Honor an explicit sys.print_exception stream without sys stdfiles.

mp_sys_print_exception only used its optional stream argument when both MICROPY_PY_IO and
MICROPY_PY_SYS_STDFILES were enabled. A small embedded port can provide StringIO while deliberately
omitting the global stdin/stdout/stderr objects, yet the explicit stream remains fully usable.

Gate explicit stream handling only on MICROPY_PY_IO. Keep the platform printer as the one-argument
fallback when sys stdfiles are absent. This restores emergency-exception and heap-locked traceback
capture without requiring console stream objects in the Capstone domain port.

diff --git i/py/modsys.c w/py/modsys.c
index 3dae92681..5e36681d9 100644
--- i/py/modsys.c
+++ w/py/modsys.c
@@ -203,10 +203,14 @@ static mp_obj_t mp_sys_print_exception(size_t n_args, const mp_obj_t *args) {
-    #if MICROPY_PY_IO && MICROPY_PY_SYS_STDFILES
-    void *stream_obj = &mp_sys_stdout_obj;
+    #if MICROPY_PY_IO
     if (n_args > 1) {
         mp_get_stream_raise(args[1], MP_STREAM_OP_WRITE);
-        stream_obj = MP_OBJ_TO_PTR(args[1]);
+        mp_print_t print = {MP_OBJ_TO_PTR(args[1]), mp_stream_write_adaptor};
+        mp_obj_print_exception(&print, args[0]);
+    } else {
+        #if MICROPY_PY_SYS_STDFILES
+        mp_print_t print = {&mp_sys_stdout_obj, mp_stream_write_adaptor};
+        mp_obj_print_exception(&print, args[0]);
+        #else
+        mp_obj_print_exception(&mp_plat_print, args[0]);
+        #endif
     }
-
-    mp_print_t print = {stream_obj, mp_stream_write_adaptor};
-    mp_obj_print_exception(&print, args[0]);
     #else
